              "Navarro’s comments suggest the Trump administration will move forward with tariffs but that it could impose penalties on a smaller group of products than those included on the original list of about 1,300.\n\nAfter the public had a chance to weigh in, the original list is expected to remain largely intact but will be slightly reduced from what was first proposed, according to two sources briefed on the plans",
              "But others say it’s still too soon to tell if Trump will move forward with actually imposing the penalties. Instead, he may choose to use the publication of the list on Friday as the latest shot across China’s bow.\n\n“I see the sword being raised. I just don’t think there’s any indication about what would really make it drop,” said Kennedy of CSIS",
              "The authorizing statute for the tariffs, Section 301 of the 1974 Trade Act, allows the Office of the U.S. Trade Representative to take up to 30 days to put the duties in place after a formal determination is published in the Federal Register. So far, USTR has not published that determination"
            ]
